{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14268644,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57976,"firstName":"Thomas","lastName":"Walker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO4EsD4gcTFRx9701mbmpsi","sequenceId":16},"course":{"id":145,"name":"Mathematics for Machine Learning"},"topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T15:02:39.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T16:09:27.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T16:11:08.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T16:11:19.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62392137,"created":"2026-10-16T16:09:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15756,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 4:09 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":81365,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":12683,"text":"<p>Simplify the statement $\\neg[\\neg (A \\land \\neg (\\neg B))] \\lor B.$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\land B) \\lor B$","choice2":"$(A \\land \\neg B) \\lor B$","choice3":"$(\\neg A \\land B) \\lor B$","choice4":"$\\neg(A \\land B) \\lor B$","choice5":"$(\\neg A \\land  \\neg B) \\lor B$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $\\neg (\\neg B)$ to $B.$ </p>\n<p>As a result of this, the statement simplifes to </p>\n<p>\\[\n\\neg (\\neg (A \\land B)) \\lor B.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can simplify $\\neg (\\neg (A \\land B))$ to $A \\land B.$</p>\n<p>Therefore, the given statement can be simplified to </p>\n<p>\\[\n(A \\land B) \\lor B.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12683,"title":"Simplifying a Double Negation"},"group":{"id":244